tags: attach

A setting of a device: when the node attaches the device.

The value is the modes that the service accepts, in the order that it prefers,
separated by commas. The modes are start (the node attaches the device before the
instance starts) and request (the instance asks for it with DeviceChange.Attach).
Example: request,start. The order has a meaning. A repeated mode is not valid.

With no setting, the mode is start. The node is bound: it uses the first mode of the
list that it supports, or refuses the service.

=== formal
class=setting
default=start
name=attach
place=service.container.devices.policies
request=the node attaches the device when the instance asks with DeviceChange.Attach, and detaches it when the instance asks
start=the node attaches the device before the instance starts; the instance has it until it stops or hibernates
value=the accepted modes, in the order of preference, separated by commas, with no repeat
values=request,start
